# The bytes a release froze, one line each as sha256sum writes it: the
# SHA-256, two spaces, the path from the repository's root. checks/frozen.sh
# fails when a file listed here is gone or holds other bytes, so what version 1
# froze cannot be edited in place by a later commit (STORAGE.md §4.2, §4.4,
# §6, §15.3).
#
# Empty while every part is a draft. The commit releasing a part adds, with
# `bash checks/frozen.sh . --digest <path...>`:
#
# storage-v1.0.0
#   migrations/storage/0001_init.sql
#   payloads/*.v1.schema.json
# sync-v1.0.0
#   vectors/sync/*.json (every case the release holds, one file each, so a
#   minor version adds a case and moves none)
#   vectors/schema/sync.schema.json
# search-v1.0.0
#   vectors/search/store.json
#   every fixture a file of vectors/search/ names
#   vectors/schema/search-*.schema.json
#   and, with `python3 checks/appended.py . --digest <path> <pointer...>`, a
#   line `<sha256>  <path> <pointer>=<count>...` for each case file:
#   vectors/search/queries.json /cases /occurrences, and refresh.json,
#   chunks.json and extraction.json /cases. checks/appended.py holds each to
#   the cases its release held as an intact prefix, the file's other fields
#   unchanged, so a minor version appends cases and edits none. The schemas
#   keep their names: a case file's format, its `v` and its schema, is frozen
#   with it, so a minor appends only cases its schema accepts, and a case
#   needing a field it lacks goes in a new file under a schema of its own.
#
# A line leaves this file only with the major version that drops its file.
